<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Campo Formio</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1797</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-first-coalition">War of the First Coalition</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Campo Formio, signed in October 1797, ended the war between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and the French Republic after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s Italian campaign. Austria ceded the Austrian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> and recognised French aims on the left bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>, while receiving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>, whose republic had been abolished, along with Istria and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> took the Venetian Ionian Islands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-campo-formio.jpg" alt="Treaty of Campo Formio" width="320" height="515" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Trait%C3%A9_de_Campo-Formio_12_sur_12_-_Archives_Nationales_-_AE-III-50bis.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
